Here's a structured explanation of the laws of thermodynamics in an interactive textbook format:

```html
<div class="interactive-textbook">
  <!-- Introduction Card -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-title">Thermodynamics Fundamentals</h2>
    <div class="card-content">
      <p>Thermodynamics studies energy transformations in physical systems. Its four fundamental laws govern all energy interactions, from microscopic particles to stars.</p>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <span class="icon">⚖️</span> Core principle: Energy conservation and entropy dictate system behavior
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Zeroth Law Card -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-title">Zeroth Law: Thermal Equilibrium</h2>
    <div class="card-content">
      <p>If two systems are separately in thermal equilibrium with a third system, they must be in equilibrium with each other.</p>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <div class="formula">\( T_A = T_B \) and \( T_B = T_C \) ⇒ \( T_A = T_C \)</div>
        <p class="formula-explanation">Establishes temperature as a valid physical property and enables temperature measurement</p>
      </div>
      <div class="characteristics">
        <h4>Key Implications:</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Defines temperature quantitatively</li>
          <li>Allows thermometer calibration</li>
          <li>Forms basis for temperature scales (Celsius, Kelvin)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- First Law Card -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-title">First Law: Energy Conservation</h2>
    <div class="card-content">
      <p>Energy cannot be created or destroyed - only converted between forms (heat, work, internal energy).</p>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <div class="formula">\( \Delta U = Q - W \)</div>
        <div class="formula-lab">
          <button class="lab-btn">Explain Symbols</button>
          <div class="lab-panel">
            <p>\( \Delta U \): Change in internal energy</p>
            <p>\( Q \): Heat added <em>to</em> system</p>
            <p>\( W \): Work done <em>by</em> system</p>
          </div>
          <button class="lab-btn">Sign Convention</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="example">
        <h4>Real-World Application:</h4>
        <p>Car engines: Convert chemical energy (fuel) → heat → mechanical work (sign convention: work <em>by</em> system is positive)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Second Law Card -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-title">Second Law: Entropy Principle</h2>
    <div class="card-content">
      <p>Natural processes increase the total entropy (disorder) of the universe.</p>

      <div class="formula-card">
        <div class="formula">\( \Delta S_{\text{univ}} \geq 0 \)</div>
        <div class="formula-lab">
          <button class="lab-btn">Clausius Statement</button>
          <div class="lab-panel">
            <p>Heat cannot spontaneously flow from cold to hot objects</p>
          </div>
          <button class="lab-btn">Kelvin Statement</button>
          <div class="lab-panel">
            <p>Impossible to convert heat completely into work</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="table-card">
        <h4>Entropy Changes in Processes</h4>
        <table class="responsive-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Process</th>
              <th>ΔS<sub>system</sub></th>
              <th>ΔS<sub>surroundings</sub></th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Ice melting</td>
              <td>+</td>
              <td>-</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Gas expansion</td>
              <td>+</td>
              <td>0</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Heat transfer</td>
              <td>-Q/T</td>
              <td>+Q/T</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Third Law Card -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-title">Third Law: Absolute Zero</h2>
    <div class="card-content">
      <p>As temperature approaches absolute zero, the entropy of a perfect crystal approaches zero.</p>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <div class="formula">\( \lim_{T \to 0} S = 0 \)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="key-concept">
        <span class="icon">❄️</span> Consequence: Absolute zero (0 K) cannot be physically reached
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Summary Table Card -->
  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-title">Laws of Thermodynamics Overview</h2>
    <div class="table-card">
      <table class="responsive-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Law</th>
            <th>Core Principle</th>
            <th>Mathematical Expression</th>
            <th>Practical Implication</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Zeroth</td>
            <td>Thermal equilibrium</td>
            <td>Transitive property of temperature</td>
            <td>Temperature measurement</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>First</td>
            <td>Energy conservation</td>
            <td>ΔU = Q - W</td>
            <td>Energy accounting</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Second</td>
            <td>Entropy increase</td>
            <td>ΔS<sub>univ</sub> ≥ 0</td>
            <td>Process directionality</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Third</td>
            <td>Absolute zero limit</td>
            <td>S → 0 as T → 0</td>
            <td>Unattainability of 0 K</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Interactive Challenge -->
  <div class="card interactive">
    <h2 class="card-title">Apply Your Knowledge</h2>
    <div class="challenge">
      <p>A refrigerator moves 300 J of heat from 4°C to 30°C. Does this violate the Second Law?</p>
      <button class="solution-btn">Reveal Analysis</button>
      <div class="solution">
        <p>No - while heat flows from cold to hot, the refrigerator requires work input (increasing surroundings' entropy). Net ΔS<sub>univ</sub> > 0.</p>
        <div class="formula">\( \Delta S_{\text{cold}} = \frac{-300}{277} \), \( \Delta S_{\text{hot}} = \frac{+300}{303} \), \( \Delta S_{\text{comp}} > 0 \)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

